<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC ROLLOVER GOOD IF QUOTAS ADHERED TO - NAIMI.</title>
<headline>OPEC ROLLOVER GOOD IF QUOTAS ADHERED TO - NAIMI.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabian oil minister Ali bin Ibrahim al-Naimi said on Tuesday that a rollover of the producer group's current ceiling would be good if all members adhered to production quotas.</p>
<p>He also told reporters that the oil market can support current OPEC output.</p>
<p>&quot;A rollover is good if everyone adheres to their quota,&quot; Naimi said.</p>
<p>OPEC ministers are scheduled to open their summer conference on Wednesday to agree production quotas for the remainder of the year.</p>
<p>The group's current ceiling is 25.033 million barrels per day (bpd) although actual output is some two million bpd above that.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand is good. There is no reason for prices to go lower,&quot; Naimi added.</p>
<p>North Sea Brent Blend crude oil prices are currently around $18 per barrel, having been closer to $25 earlier this year.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
